{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonMTCInput","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonMTCInput","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L115-L120","doc":"**The value-step ratio, categorically:** `S_{0λ}/S_{00} = catQDim λ` — the categorical quantum\ndimension of the `λ`-th simple object. This is `bwS0` recognised as the Verlinde vacuum row of the\n*Mathlib* ribbon category, the content input (RT) supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_vac","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The vacuum entry is `S_{00} = 1/D` (the vacuum object's categorical dimension is `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_eq_catQDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vacuumRow_S0_eq_catQDim","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L103-L107","doc":"**The modular S-matrix vacuum row of the RT input is the categorical quantum dimension,\nnormalized.** `S_{0λ} = catQDim λ / D` — the value `bwS0` must equal, now grounded in Mathlib's\nbraided-rigid categorical dimension rather than an abstract field element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.toVerlindeVacuumRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.toVerlindeVacuumRow","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L94-L101","doc":"The RT input assembles into a `VerlindeVacuumRow` whose quantum dimension is the categorical\n`catQDim`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.catQDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.catQDim","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The base-ring quantum dimension `d_λ = evalUnit(qDimObj (S λ))` — the categorical dimension of\nthe `λ`-th simple object, evaluated into `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vac_dim_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vac_dim_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The vacuum object has categorical quantum dimension `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.D_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.D_ne","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L82-L82","doc":"`D ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.D","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Total quantum dimension `D = √(Σ d²)` (abstract; only `D ≠ 0` used). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.vac","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The vacuum (trivial-object) label. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.evalUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.evalUnit","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The scalar evaluation `End(𝟙_C) → R` (the ribbon category's ground-ring identification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.S","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The simple objects indexed by the fusion labels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.RibbonMTCInput","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L67-L84","doc":"**RT input over a Mathlib ribbon category.** The data the Reshetikhin–Turaev construction needs\nto produce the vacuum row `bwS0`: a family of simple objects `S : ι → C` (the fusion labels), a\nscalar evaluation `evalUnit : End(𝟙_C) → R` (the ribbon category's `End(𝟙_C) ≅ R`), a total\nquantum dimension `D ≠ 0`, and the vacuum object of categorical quantum dimension `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.qDimObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RibbonMTC.qDimObj","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneRibbonMTCInput.lean#L54-L65","doc":"**The categorical (right) quantum dimension** of an object `X` in a braided right-rigid\ncategory, as an endomorphism of the unit object: the *braided*, **twistless** closure of the\nidentity, `𝟙_C --η_X--> X ⊗ Xᘁ --β--> Xᘁ ⊗ X --ε_X--> 𝟙_C`.  This is the `dim_q(X) ∈ End(𝟙_C)` that\nthe abstract `VerlindeVacuumRow.d` stands for.\n\n**Not the ribbon trace** (a borrowed name this docstring used to carry): the ribbon trace carries\nthe balancing twist and there is no `BalancedCategory` in the variable block above, so no `θ`\nappears here and none can.  See `QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedWith` for the twisted version.  Nothing\ndownstream of this definition is affected — `qDim_unit` and the vacuum-row results are true of the\nobject actually defined here, and since `θ_𝟙 = 𝟙` they read the same either way. ","signatureChunk":0}]}